WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:22.220
An ankle scope procedure, also known as ankle
arthroscopy, can be used to treat conditions

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:28.310
that cause pain or decreased flexibility of
the ankle joint.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:32.180
The ankle is the joint that connects the leg
and the foot.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:39.780
The ankle joint includes the two lower leg
bones, called the tibia and the fibula, and

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.300
the ankle bone, called the talus.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:53.580
Together the ends of the tibia and the fibula
create a mortis, or a slot, for the talus.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:59.300
Tissues called ligaments and tendons support
the ankle bones.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:07.400
Ligaments attach bones to bones and tendons
attach muscles to bones.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:13.189
The ankle joint allows the foot to move up
and down.

00:01:13.189 --> 00:01:18.430
Articular cartilage on the ends of bones is
a smooth gliding covering that allows fluid

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.640
joint movement.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:27.770
A variety of conditions can cause pain or
decreased flexibility of the ankle joint.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.790
Abnormal bone growths, called bone spurs,
may have formed, impinging on the ankle joint

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.110
as it moves.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:43.870
Ligaments may be damaged, either from overuse
or from ankle injuries, such sprains. Old

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:49.490
ankle injuries may stretch the ligaments,
allowing abnormal movement of the ankle joint.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:57.130
This can lead to more rapid degenerative changes
in the joint.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:05.760
Cartilage may be damaged or worn thin due
to prior ankle injury or osteoarthritis.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.670
Small pieces of cartilage may have detached
from the underlying bone and may be floating

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.590
in the joint.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:18.720
The joint space may be infected, usually from
bacteria.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:26.560
To treat these and other conditions, a surgeon
may perform an ankle scope.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:32.220
The surgeon will begin by making several tiny
incisions, or portals, in the ankle.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:38.580
A small tube called a cannula will be placed
into one of the incisions.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.310
A scope will be passed through the cannula
to allow the surgeon to see inside the joint

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.970
area.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.590
The scope contains a tiny camera that will
project the image of the ankle joint onto

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.590
a TV monitor for the surgeon to watch.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:59.870
A sterile saline solution will be pumped through
the scoped cannula, to expand the area so

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:05.930
the surgeon can see better and have more area
in which to work.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.490
The surgeon will insert surgical instruments
into the other incision to do one or more

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.090
of the following treatments.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:18.430
A bone spur will be removed or burred down.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:23.970
Excess tissue will be removed from a thick
scarred ligament.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:31.000
Loose pieces of cartilage floating in the
joint will be removed.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:40.410
Infection in the ankle joint will be cleaned
out by washing the joint with fluid.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:47.900
If a person has damaged cartilage or bone
from arthritis, ankle fusion will be performed.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:55.990
During an ankle fusion damaged cartilage and
bone will be removed.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:02.230
The bones will be attached to each other with
screws.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:07.290
This will lock the ankle joint in one position
while other joints in the foot will continue

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.940
to allow limited movement.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:16.440
Once the treatment is finished the sterile
saline will be drilled out of the joint, the

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.529
instruments will be removed, and the incisions
will be closed with stitches.

